  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThese guidelines help ensure that content on the heart failure portal is accurate, appropriately targeted and easy to maintain.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBefore Publishing\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBefore publishing, confirm that:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe author name, category, content type and page title are correct.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EVisibility is set to the intended audience.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe overview accurately summarises the page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClinical content has been approved by a suitably qualified reviewer.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EReferences and external links are current and working.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHeadings, tables and images display correctly, and images include meaningful alternative text.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe page contains no identifiable patient information or confidential data.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECopyright permissions have been obtained for third-party material.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ERecommended Workflow\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EDraft:\u003C/strong\u003E The author creates the content and saves it without publishing.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EReview:\u003C/strong\u003E A subject matter expert checks accuracy, and an editor checks clarity and formatting.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EApproval:\u003C/strong\u003E The reviewer records their approval and any required changes.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPublish:\u003C/strong\u003E An administrator publishes the page and checks it using an account for the intended role.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EMaintain:\u003C/strong\u003E The page is reviewed on schedule and whenever guidance changes.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EContent Review\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClinical content should be reviewed at least every 12 months or sooner if new evidence, safety alerts or guideline changes occur. Pages that are no longer accurate should be updated or unpublished promptly.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccess and Version Control\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAccess should follow the principle of least privilege, with staff only given the permissions needed for their role. Accounts should be removed or changed when responsibilities change. Major edits should be recorded in the version history, including the reason for the change and who approved it.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessibility and Reporting\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPages should also meet accessibility requirements, including logical heading order, descriptive link text and sufficient colour contrast. Report suspected errors or privacy incidents to the portal owner immediately.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </bodyContent>
